<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shamshi-Adad I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1808–1776 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shamshi-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadad">Adad</a> I was an Amorite ruler who reigned c. 1808–1776 BCE and built a kingdom across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, including the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a>. He is regarded as an important figure in early Assyrian history. His kingdom collapsed after his death, opening the way for the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shamshi-adad-i.jpg" alt="Shamshi-Adad I" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adelheid Otto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shamshi-Adad_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
